Stack: Project SelectionPurpose:  Project-specific technology stack selections. These files are selected  instances from the root .sdd/stack/ technology catalog. Each selection  is documented with rationale and alternative choices.  Stack templates live at @../../../templates/_sdd/stack/.Owns: ./ReadOrder:   1  @INDEX.sdd (this file ? project stack map)   2  @LAYER.template.sdd (stack layer template)   3  @<layer>.sdd (specific layer selection, when populated)Modes:  ANALYZE   ? stack fit and compatibility analysis  PLAN      ? technology selection and mapping  WORK      ? stack-based implementation  VERIFY    ? stack compliance check  REVIEW    ? technology decision executionRules:  [PS1]  Project stack MUST be selected from root .sdd/stack/ catalog.  [PS2]  Technology selection MUST be recorded with rationale.  [PS3]  Stack compatibility (all layers) MUST be validated.  [PS4]  Version policy MUST follow root stack/ guidelines.  [PS5]  Technology changes require TECH_UPDATE_PROPOSAL.  [PS6]  Cross-layer impact MUST be analyzed on stack changes.Entry:  Read:    INDEX.sdd  Resolve:    backend    frontend    mobile    database    testing    infrastructureNavigation:  ProjectStack: @projects/{project_name}/stack/INDEX.sdd  Backend: @projects/{project_name}/stack/backend.sdd  Frontend: @projects/{project_name}/stack/frontend.sdd  Mobile: @projects/{project_name}/stack/mobile.sdd  Database: @projects/{project_name}/stack/database.sdd  Testing: @projects/{project_name}/stack/testing.sdd  Infrastructure: @projects/{project_name}/stack/infrastructure.sdd  RootStack: @stack/INDEX.sdd  Template: @../../../templates/_sdd/stack/LAYER.template.sddState: +Note:  This file is the project-specific stack map. It points to  detailed stack files and references the root stack knowledge base.  Concrete stack selections are generated per project by the  project-structure skill from templates/_sdd/stack/.

